# Code Review — {{project_name}}

<!-- GEN: Why: the order of passes, verification gates, and verdict criteria must be fixed so every review is deterministic and reproducible. Kind: Mandatory — keep the purpose, adapt the structure (core/authoring-guide.md). -->

Reviewer is strictly read-only toward implementation, tests, schemas, and dependencies; write review reports only.

## 1. CLI & Validator Verification Gates (`PASS` / `FAIL`)

| Gate | Command / Tool | Pass Criteria |
|---|---|---|
| **Architecture / Boundary Check** | `{{arch_validator_cmd}}` | `PASS` (zero `ERROR` / boundary breaches) |
| **Static Analysis & Lint** | `{{lint_cmd}}` | `PASS` (`exit 0`) |
| **Type Check** | `{{typecheck_cmd}}` | `PASS` (`exit 0`) |
| **Independent Test Suite** | `{{test_cmd}}` | `PASS` (all tests green on `REVIEW_REVISION`) |

`NOT_RUN`, `BLOCKED`, and `UNVERIFIED` never count as `PASS`.

## 2. Order of Passes

1. **Fix the revision & rerun gates (`R1`, `R2`, `R6`):** Record `BASE_REVISION..REVIEW_REVISION` and uncommitted scope; rerun the hand-off's checks and AC commands yourself ([01 — Scope, Gates & Validators]({{ref_01}})).
2. **Bug-hunt first (`R3`):** Run `{{bug_hunt_link}}` cold at `standard` (or `deep` for high-risk items) before reading design documents.
3. **Grade the 5 review axes (`R4`, `R5`):** Audit Plan/AC traceability, Architecture, Code Quality/Simplicity, Adversarial Tests (`TEST-TAMPER-001`), and Security/Contracts/UI against the rubric skills ([02 — Review Axes & Rubric]({{ref_02}})).
4. **Write findings & decide verdict (`R7`–`R14`):** Grade findings with `BLOCKER` / `MAJOR` / `MINOR`, apply no-waiver verdict rules (`APPROVED` / `CHANGES_REQUESTED` / `BLOCKED`), and write the revision-bound report ([03 — Findings, Verdict & Report]({{ref_03}})).

## 3. Mandatory Rules (`R1`–`R14`)

| ID | Rule Summary | Reference |
|---|---|---|
| **R1–R3, R6, R9** | Fixed revision, strictly read-only, bug-hunt first, rerun checks independently, diff + broken callers scope | [01 — Scope, Gates & Validators]({{ref_01}}) |
| **R4–R5** | Grade axes with workspace rubric skills, trace every AC, reject happy-path-only or tampered tests (`TEST-TAMPER-001`) | [02 — Review Axes & Rubric]({{ref_02}}) |
| **R7–R8, R10–R14** | No reviewer waivers (`PLAN_CONFLICT`), actionable `RV-NN` rows, verdict criteria, 3-round cap, delta re-review, report | [03 — Findings, Verdict & Report]({{ref_03}}) |

